The KC868-A16 supports both **Ethernet (LAN8720 PHY)** and **WiFi**. ESPHome enforces XOR — exactly one transport is active per device. Pick one in MajiFlow's *Connection* panel; the choice is baked into the firmware at flash time.

| | Ethernet | WiFi |
|---|---|---|
| **Default for this board** | ✓ | |
| **Speed / reliability** | Wired, deterministic | Depends on RF environment |
| **Credentials needed** | None | SSID + password |
| **Diagnostic sensor** | `ethernet_info` (IP) | `wifi_info` (IP, SSID, MAC) + `wifi_signal` (dBm) |
| **Static IP support** | ✓ via *Connection → IP Configuration* | ✓ same panel |
| **Fallback when network is down** | **None** — device is unreachable until cable is replugged | SoftAP starts automatically |

### Recovery path on WiFi transport

When the configured WiFi network is unreachable, ESPHome activates a fallback hotspot after **~90 seconds** of failed station association ([`wifi.ap_timeout`](https://esphome.io/components/wifi.html) default). MajiFlow does not currently override this — if you need faster recovery during commissioning, edit the generated YAML to add `wifi.ap_timeout: 30s` before flashing.

- **SoftAP SSID**: `<friendly_name> Fallback` — derived from the device's friendly name in MajiFlow. For example, a device named *Pump Controller* broadcasts as `Pump Controller Fallback`.
- **SoftAP password**: identical to your `wifi_password` — one credential to remember.
- **Default gateway**: **`192.168.4.1`** — connect your phone/laptop to the SoftAP first, then the OS pops the captive-portal page automatically (Android/iOS detect it via `/generate_204`, `/hotspot-detect.html`, etc.). Use it to **re-enter WiFi credentials** (`/wifisave`) or **push an OTA firmware update** (`/update`). Note: typing `http://192.168.4.1/` directly may land on the entity dashboard instead of the wifi-recovery page — this is a known ESPHome ordering quirk ([#11132](https://github.com/esphome/esphome/issues/11132), [#14856](https://github.com/esphome/esphome/issues/14856)) where `web_server`'s catch-all shadows the captive-portal index. The captive-portal *routes* still work; just navigate via the OS popup.

### Recovery path on Ethernet transport

There is no on-device recovery. Options:

1. Plug the cable back in.
2. Switch transport to WiFi in MajiFlow → re-flash → use the WiFi fallback above.

### Web dashboard

Always emitted on **port 80** alongside the chosen transport. Reachable at:

- `http://<device-ip>/` on the home network — the IP shown in `ethernet_info` or `wifi_info`.
- `http://192.168.4.1/` on the fallback AP — but entity controls won't function until WiFi rejoins (no STA = no time, no MQTT, no API). Use the captive-portal popup for credential reset; come back to the dashboard at the home-network IP after the device reconnects.

Every relay, sensor, switch, and number entity declared in the topology is exposed for manual control — nothing extra to configure.
